# F-014 remediation item 5: documented, time-bounded exceptions for
# accepted Trivy findings (filesystem + IaC config scans). Referenced by
# .github/workflows/security-scan.yml via --ignorefile .trivyignore.
#
# Format (see https://trivy.dev/latest/docs/configuration/filtering/#by-finding-ids):
#   CVE-2024-XXXXX exp:2026-12-31
#
# Every entry MUST have:
#   1. The CVE/advisory ID or Trivy check ID being suppressed.
#   2. An `exp:YYYY-MM-DD` expiry date. Trivy stops honoring an entry once
#      its expiry date passes, so an unreviewed exception fails the scan
#      again automatically rather than suppressing a finding forever by
#      accident.
#   3. A comment on the line above explaining why it's accepted and who
#      approved it -- "add an exception" must be an explicit, reviewed,
#      time-bounded decision (remediation item 5), not a way to make this
#      gate quietly stop mattering.
#
# No entries yet -- add one only with a real justification and expiry,
# reviewed the same way any other change to this file would be (this file
# is not exempt from normal code review).
